WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.011
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:10.281 --> 00:11.491
Please come in.

3
00:11.991 --> 00:16.287
SOME TIME AGO

4
00:20.041 --> 00:22.001
I'll reschedule your doctor's appointment.

5
00:29.509 --> 00:30.927
It's been a while, Director.

6
00:35.932 --> 00:36.975
Indeed.

7
00:40.854 --> 00:42.397
Remember him?

8
00:48.987 --> 00:50.321
Your son has grown up well.

9
00:54.450 --> 00:55.827
From what I hear,

10
00:57.120 --> 01:00.290
he's been going around killing people.

11
01:08.131 --> 01:10.508
And why are you telling me this?

12
01:13.052 --> 01:15.138
Kill him for me.

13
01:18.099 --> 01:20.268
Before it gets out of hand.

14
01:20.894 --> 01:24.022
You can make it look like an accident.

15
01:24.522 --> 01:26.566
Or I guess you could have a cop do it.

16
01:26.649 --> 01:27.984
With all due respect, sir,

17
01:29.611 --> 01:30.987
why would I?

18
01:33.823 --> 01:35.074
I'll be going now.

19
01:36.034 --> 01:38.828
He administers Speed K

20
01:40.330 --> 01:44.876
before killing people by twisting their limbs, or so I hear.

21
01:46.920 --> 01:48.421
Speaking of which,

22
01:49.672 --> 01:52.842
you developed that drug, did you not?

23
01:58.640 --> 02:02.977
Are you really just going to sit back and watch our secrets from back then

24
02:03.478 --> 02:04.938
come to light?

25
02:06.397 --> 02:09.943
It's thanks to those days that we're here now.

26
02:22.288 --> 02:23.122
Then,

27
02:24.040 --> 02:26.376
if I kill your son for you…

28
02:29.212 --> 02:31.589
please help my business in return.

29
03:26.644 --> 03:28.521
THE BLUE ROAD

30
03:35.153 --> 03:35.987
Seok.

31
03:40.658 --> 03:41.534
What is it?

32
03:42.327 --> 03:44.620
Do you still hear the bells, even after the rite?

33
03:45.621 --> 03:46.706
So,

34
03:47.290 --> 03:48.291
are you afraid?

35
03:49.334 --> 03:50.960
That the calling won't stop?

36
03:56.632 --> 03:57.467
Yes.

37
03:59.594 --> 04:00.803
I'm scared.

38
04:04.640 --> 04:05.725
I never know

39
04:07.268 --> 04:09.354
when I'll hear the bells rattle again.

40
04:10.313 --> 04:12.940
You're only scared because you keep thinking it's scary.

41
04:16.319 --> 04:17.195
But

42
04:18.321 --> 04:22.867
what if you thought of it as a lifelong friend or a brother?

43
04:24.660 --> 04:26.371
Then it wouldn't seem so scary.

44
04:27.038 --> 04:29.499
In fact, it'll stay right by your side

45
04:29.999 --> 04:31.167
and protect you.

46
04:33.836 --> 04:35.213
Just like I always will.

47
04:39.592 --> 04:41.094
Don't be afraid.

48
04:44.889 --> 04:46.391
Don't be afraid.

49
04:49.769 --> 04:50.978
Don't be afraid…

50
04:57.235 --> 04:59.445
Let's move seats. Come on.

51
05:42.822 --> 05:44.073
Snap out of it.

52
05:49.412 --> 05:50.621
Snap out of it!

53
06:00.339 --> 06:01.466
Seo Hyun-tae.

54
06:03.050 --> 06:04.177
Minamoto.

55
06:05.344 --> 06:07.930
Minamoto Shunsuke. Hong Du-yeong.

56
06:21.611 --> 06:26.741
INCHEON PORT, CHEONGHAE SHIPYARD THE MIRAE, 21:00

57
06:32.705 --> 06:35.458
Cheonghae Shipyard, The Mirae. Cheonghae Shipyard.

58
06:36.876 --> 06:37.919
The Mirae.

59
06:52.725 --> 06:55.061
PROFESSOR JANG, THIS IS KIM SEOK

60
06:55.144 --> 06:58.314
I'M WRITING TO ASK FOR A FAVOR YOU'RE THE ONLY ONE I CAN TRUST

61
07:08.324 --> 07:10.284
Inspector Kim, you inside?

62
07:13.955 --> 07:16.040
Kim Seok, you inside or what?

63
07:20.836 --> 07:22.088
Yes, I'm here. One second.

64
07:39.814 --> 07:41.232
Fuck.

65
07:41.315 --> 07:42.316
Kim Seok!

66
07:42.817 --> 07:43.651
Freeze.

67
07:44.986 --> 07:45.987
You.

68
08:01.752 --> 08:04.255
That fucking lunatic. The window!

69
08:11.178 --> 08:14.140
Ha In-beom! Where are you? Did you get him?

70
08:15.766 --> 08:16.642
In-beom.

71
08:16.726 --> 08:19.186
Someone reported you as a drug offender.

72
08:22.440 --> 08:25.109
For drug use, distribution, and even smuggling.

73
08:27.903 --> 08:28.863
And you believe that?

74
08:28.946 --> 08:31.198
Of course I don't, but what choice do I have?!

75
08:31.949 --> 08:34.827
The report came in, and they want us to investigate you.

76
08:36.037 --> 08:38.497
It's not like I want to do this!

77
08:52.803 --> 08:53.929
Come on, kid.

78
08:56.015 --> 08:57.683
What kind of idiot cop

79
08:58.809 --> 09:01.020
sympathizes with a suspect?

80
09:01.937 --> 09:04.857
You're not just some suspect.

81
09:07.568 --> 09:08.694
Forget it.

82
09:20.706 --> 09:22.667
Where did he go?!

83
09:23.292 --> 09:25.044
Kim Seok! Where'd he go?! Damn it.

84
09:29.715 --> 09:31.550
Did you lose him or let him go?

85
09:34.053 --> 09:35.179
Great job.

86
09:36.639 --> 09:37.890
Damn it.

87
09:41.435 --> 09:44.438
I'm spending a fortune on flights.

88
09:45.648 --> 09:47.650
I'll bill you for all of it.

89
09:51.696 --> 09:55.199
Inose. I know you're in there. Open up.

90
10:00.955 --> 10:02.832
Hey, Inose. Open up.

91
10:14.051 --> 10:16.512
How do you know my passcode?

92
10:17.221 --> 10:18.806
Pardon my intrusion.

93
10:21.600 --> 10:23.227
Zero, five, two, nine.

94
10:23.728 --> 10:26.021
It's Rumi's birthday.

95
10:34.739 --> 10:38.033
I switched to a digital door lock

96
10:38.659 --> 10:41.078
so it would be easier for Rumi to come visit.

97
10:43.914 --> 10:46.000
Why are you taking those out?

98
10:51.172 --> 10:53.299
Where are you off to this time?

99
10:59.722 --> 11:03.058
So, why did you come all the way to my place?

100
11:03.559 --> 11:05.561
Did the Korean security service tell you to?

101
11:07.438 --> 11:09.356
Inspector Kim Seok…

102
11:13.527 --> 11:14.612
Detective Kim?

103
11:15.613 --> 11:18.115
Looks like he's been put on Korea's wanted list.

104
11:20.618 --> 11:21.702
On what charge?

105
11:21.786 --> 11:24.914
For violating the Narcotics Control Act.

106
11:25.915 --> 11:28.751
And it looks like he's on the run to avoid investigation.

107
11:32.838 --> 11:34.673
Speed K…

108
11:41.806 --> 11:45.142
Ito Makoto, Minamoto Pharmaceuticals,

109
11:45.643 --> 11:47.311
Japanese and Korean intelligence…

110
11:50.606 --> 11:52.399
This is on a whole other scale.

111
11:52.900 --> 11:56.237
Just who the hell was this Minamoto Shunsuke anyway?

112
11:58.072 --> 12:00.032
Inose, think about it!

113
12:00.658 --> 12:04.912
If a Korean agent was here, it means higher-ups on both sides are watching.

114
12:04.995 --> 12:08.332
Which means if you do anything rash,

115
12:08.833 --> 12:12.586
it could affect your ex-wife and even Rumi--

116
12:12.670 --> 12:14.880
Don't you dare say something like that!

117
12:16.715 --> 12:17.591
Inose.

118
12:18.551 --> 12:19.844
You're suspended.

119
12:21.303 --> 12:24.890
Come into the station tomorrow and turn in your gun.

120
12:26.684 --> 12:28.477
This is your final warning.

121
12:28.978 --> 12:30.604
Do not go to Korea!

122
12:30.688 --> 12:33.732
In fact, don't do anything for the time being.

123
12:36.527 --> 12:40.739
You love playing pachinko. Go kill some time doing that instead.

124
12:50.833 --> 12:55.087
CHEONGHAE SHIPYARD

125
13:21.363 --> 13:22.573
Is this the Mirae?

126
13:35.586 --> 13:37.046
Where is this headed?

127
13:52.436 --> 13:55.773
Should I quit being a detective and try my hand at pachinko?

128
14:06.200 --> 14:07.993
Incredible!

129
14:09.286 --> 14:10.454
This is bad.

130
14:12.539 --> 14:14.291
Here, guys. Take some.

131
14:19.463 --> 14:21.340
Sir.

132
14:21.423 --> 14:23.717
Sorry to interrupt you while you're having fun.

133
14:23.801 --> 14:25.803
Could I have a moment of your time?

134
14:28.389 --> 14:32.726
Allow me to escort you to our VIP room where there's no betting limit.

135
14:34.103 --> 14:35.479
That sounds interesting.

136
14:40.693 --> 14:44.029
-Sir, hold my spot for me. -Okay.

137
14:51.245 --> 14:52.079
Please come in.

138
14:57.626 --> 15:00.212
Sure looks like the VIP room, all right.

139
15:02.881 --> 15:05.634
So many VIPs here.

140
15:23.360 --> 15:24.528
Sir.

141
15:25.112 --> 15:30.367
I don't know how you pulled it off, but hand over your winnings and get out.

142
15:31.201 --> 15:34.455
You are now banned from the premises.

143
15:34.955 --> 15:39.043
Neither Ito nor Li Yoon-ok is here, and these walls are soundproofed.

144
15:43.839 --> 15:44.965
You.

145
15:45.883 --> 15:46.842
Who the hell are you?

146
15:48.677 --> 15:50.637
I'll cough up all my winnings.

147
15:53.015 --> 15:53.849
What?

148
15:56.101 --> 15:58.312
If you tell me about Ito.

149
16:05.944 --> 16:07.988
You're a funny guy, aren't you?

150
16:09.740 --> 16:11.450
I'm turning this in anyway, so…

151
16:16.830 --> 16:18.916
-I'll call the police! -The police?

152
16:18.999 --> 16:22.836
I am the police. Shall I clean this whole place out?

153
16:25.089 --> 16:26.298
Where is Ito?

154
16:30.135 --> 16:34.807
We're just underlings. We don't know where the boss is.

155
16:38.393 --> 16:40.771
We really don't know!

156
16:44.983 --> 16:47.361
Where is Ito? Where is he?

157
16:47.444 --> 16:50.697
Hong Kong!

158
16:52.950 --> 16:54.118
Hong Kong?

159
17:04.920 --> 17:07.923
HONG KONG

160
17:34.366 --> 17:37.327
SEO HYUN-TAE IS IN HONG KONG

161
17:37.411 --> 17:39.037
Who's helping me?

162
17:57.472 --> 17:58.348
Hello?

163
17:58.849 --> 17:59.683
Prof…

164
18:00.601 --> 18:02.394
Hello, Professor Jang. This is Kim Seok.

165
18:02.477 --> 18:03.729
Detective Kim.

166
18:04.313 --> 18:06.231
I was worried because I couldn't reach you.

167
18:06.315 --> 18:07.357
Sorry about that.

168
18:08.192 --> 18:10.277
You know the request I made via email?

169
18:10.360 --> 18:13.322
Yes, I'm at the nursing home right now.

170
18:13.822 --> 18:17.451
I said the name you mentioned to your mother, and…

171
18:17.993 --> 18:19.203
One moment.

172
18:24.666 --> 18:27.419
She started screaming and had a seizure.

173
18:27.502 --> 18:30.797
Her pulse and breathing went through the roof. It was chaos.

174
18:32.883 --> 18:35.260
She's now sleeping under sedation.

175
18:36.720 --> 18:38.889
But what's clear from your mother's reaction is…

176
18:45.187 --> 18:46.188
She seems to know him.

177
18:47.397 --> 18:49.107
This Seo Hyun-tae person.

178
18:50.651 --> 18:53.695
As soon as she heard the name, she started calling out, "Du-yeong."

179
18:53.779 --> 18:56.365
Then she had a seizure and collapsed.

180
18:57.282 --> 19:00.327
Are you actually curious how Hong Du-yeong died, or…

181
19:03.038 --> 19:05.040
are you curious why he died?

182
19:10.587 --> 19:12.047
Yes, I understand.

183
19:14.091 --> 19:16.260
Professor, I'll make sure to repay this favor.

184
19:16.343 --> 19:17.511
One moment.

185
19:18.345 --> 19:21.682
About the documents we discussed last time.

186
19:22.182 --> 19:24.351
The Tiger Unit under the Government-General.

187
19:24.935 --> 19:25.769
Yes?

188
19:26.353 --> 19:29.773
I was looking into what fellow scholars had written on the subject,

189
19:29.856 --> 19:33.485
and it seems remnants of it may have persisted

190
19:34.027 --> 19:35.988
even after the Japanese occupation.

191
19:37.739 --> 19:39.449
By remnants, what do you mean?

192
19:39.533 --> 19:44.037
The methods they used to torture people or the use of drugs, for example.

193
19:45.247 --> 19:47.374
"It is highly probable they were passed down

194
19:47.457 --> 19:51.003
to the military in preparation for war or to certain government agencies."

195
19:51.086 --> 19:54.339
"In the 1980s, for example, the Agency for National Security Planning

196
19:54.423 --> 19:59.386
operated undercover, posing as companies, factories, print shops, and the like."

197
19:59.469 --> 20:03.724
"The brutality of the acts they carried out is beyond imagination…"

198
20:03.807 --> 20:05.350
The ANSP in the '80s…

199
20:06.101 --> 20:07.102
Print shop.

200
20:08.478 --> 20:11.481
"At the time, those involved in the student and civic movements,

201
20:11.565 --> 20:14.192
including a few college students, activists,

202
20:14.276 --> 20:16.653
and even shamans involved in anti-Japanese activism,

203
20:16.737 --> 20:18.488
were arrested by the ANSP."

204
20:18.989 --> 20:23.577
They may have inherited the Tiger Unit's torture methods.

205
20:27.080 --> 20:28.248
Anti-Japanese activism?

206
20:30.834 --> 20:31.835
Shamans…

207
20:33.628 --> 20:35.339
Anti-Japanese activism, shamans…

208
20:57.569 --> 21:00.405
Inose! What the hell are you thinking?

209
21:00.906 --> 21:02.741
I told you to lay low!

210
21:02.824 --> 21:04.409
What do you mean?

211
21:04.493 --> 21:08.413
I listened to you, didn't go to Korea, and accepted my suspension.

212
21:08.497 --> 21:09.956
-What I mean is… -Come on.

213
21:10.457 --> 21:12.959
Aren't you the one who told me to go play some pachinko?

214
21:13.043 --> 21:15.295
When did I tell you to go and start trouble--

215
21:15.796 --> 21:19.883
They tried to rip me off, so I just gave them a little talking to.

216
21:19.966 --> 21:22.886
You… Honestly, Inose, I can't believe you!

217
21:23.470 --> 21:24.471
Hanging up now.

218
21:27.766 --> 21:29.935
Are you here to find Seo Hyun-tae?

219
21:34.648 --> 21:35.774
Hello.

220
21:37.192 --> 21:38.318
Why are you…

221
21:42.614 --> 21:46.410
Trouble reaching Inspector Kim Seok? I bet his hands are full right now.

222
21:46.493 --> 21:47.411
Kim Seok?

223
21:50.414 --> 21:51.373
You can reach him?

224
21:51.456 --> 21:54.876
No. Somebody else is assigned to him.

225
21:58.797 --> 22:00.257
What the hell?

226
22:01.800 --> 22:03.468
You knew I'd come here?

227
22:05.011 --> 22:06.388
Fifty-fifty, maybe?

228
22:06.471 --> 22:07.848
Fifty-fifty?

229
22:09.349 --> 22:12.686
You ignored my warning that it'd be dangerous and came anyway.

230
22:14.521 --> 22:17.858
So how about a strategic partnership?

231
22:22.988 --> 22:24.990
Where are you going? Hey!

232
22:25.490 --> 22:27.868
We have to go catch Seo Hyun-tae. Come on!

233
22:35.083 --> 22:39.588
For a long time, Hong Kong was a tax haven for countless companies.

234
22:40.088 --> 22:41.131
But

235
22:41.715 --> 22:47.012
Hong Kong's changed somewhat since the handover from the UK.

236
22:51.892 --> 22:54.895
Typical Japanese with zero interest in other countries' histories.

237
22:54.978 --> 22:56.104
Say what?

238
22:56.605 --> 22:58.106
"Say what" isn't very polite.

239
22:59.024 --> 23:00.192
"Pardon?"

240
23:03.236 --> 23:06.323
I guess you've got a lot on your mind right now.

241
23:06.406 --> 23:11.286
You must be wondering if Kim Seok's really in Hong Kong, whether he's okay.

242
23:12.829 --> 23:13.830
Actually,

243
23:14.831 --> 23:18.293
I was wondering if it's really necessary for the Korean security service

244
23:18.376 --> 23:19.294
to get involved.

245
23:27.177 --> 23:28.637
Speed K.

246
23:30.180 --> 23:31.097
What?

247
23:32.641 --> 23:35.894
Seo Hyun-tae is at the center of Northeast Asia's drug cartel.

248
23:36.478 --> 23:39.648
He's been systematically distributing drugs in Korea as well.

249
23:39.731 --> 23:42.192
We've been tracking him for years.

250
23:43.401 --> 23:46.863
Korean and Japanese intelligence, together.

251
23:49.658 --> 23:53.161
Seo Hyun-tae has been manufacturing Speed K in Central Asia

252
23:53.245 --> 23:55.705
and routing it through Hong Kong for distribution.

253
23:56.206 --> 23:58.500
But when the crackdowns intensified,

254
23:59.000 --> 24:04.381
his way around them was to turn Speed K into a legal drug.

255
24:05.966 --> 24:07.801
Like fentanyl, for instance.

256
24:22.941 --> 24:26.611
Seo Hyun-tae and Minamoto Pharmaceuticals will sign a major contract today.

257
24:27.737 --> 24:31.283
I don't know why Minamoto decided to join forces with Seo Hyun-tae,

258
24:32.200 --> 24:34.327
but there must have been some sort of deal.

259
24:35.954 --> 24:37.038
Anyway,

260
24:37.872 --> 24:40.500
we're going to catch Seo Hyun-tae tonight.

261
24:53.430 --> 24:54.514
But here's the thing.

262
24:55.515 --> 24:59.394
I'm just a detective who's chasing a serial killer.

263
25:00.145 --> 25:03.648
What do a drug investigation and an international criminal organization

264
25:03.732 --> 25:05.275
have to do with a murder case?

265
25:09.237 --> 25:12.532
Who do you think first came up with Emi Shunsuke's twisted methods?

266
25:17.287 --> 25:18.622
Seo Hyun-tae was

267
25:19.497 --> 25:20.999
a senior agent of ours.

268
25:21.583 --> 25:22.584
Senior agent?

269
25:23.293 --> 25:25.462
That's just how I'm putting it.

270
25:26.588 --> 25:27.797
In the '80s,

271
25:27.881 --> 25:32.010
he was an external contractor for the Korean ANSP.

272
25:33.553 --> 25:35.180
The so-called "print shop."

273
25:35.680 --> 25:39.100
It was kept hidden due to its extreme brutality, even by ANSP standards.

274
25:40.018 --> 25:43.772
Some say they used torture methods passed down from the Japanese colonial era.

275
25:44.731 --> 25:48.151
Twisting limb joints, a method of killing that bordered on torture.

276
25:49.653 --> 25:51.571
The person who first came up with it…

277
25:54.366 --> 25:55.700
was perhaps…

278
26:10.590 --> 26:11.424
The chairman says…

279
26:13.760 --> 26:15.553
the contract is on hold for now.

280
26:18.973 --> 26:20.934
Until the clinical trial results are in.

281
26:21.851 --> 26:25.063
So I suggest you leave quietly.

282
26:37.617 --> 26:39.744
You want to put the contract on hold

283
26:41.454 --> 26:42.997
until the trial results are in?

284
26:49.421 --> 26:50.463
Director.

285
26:52.340 --> 26:53.591
Hong Kong's nice, isn't it?

286
26:54.300 --> 26:55.927
You pay less taxes.

287
26:57.387 --> 26:58.638
A great place to rest.

288
26:58.722 --> 27:01.307
How dare you…

289
27:04.811 --> 27:07.188
Even a damn mongrel knows

290
27:08.064 --> 27:10.483
to watch its step.

291
27:20.160 --> 27:21.703
And yet you dare…

292
27:23.747 --> 27:27.709
They say a mongrel will piss itself at a single roar from a tiger.

293
27:31.963 --> 27:35.049
Listen to you, running your mouth.

294
27:36.801 --> 27:38.595
I dare you to keep talking.

295
27:39.471 --> 27:41.014
I wonder why.

296
27:42.056 --> 27:45.351
Why do I feel like I could rip your throat out…

297
27:47.353 --> 27:49.147
and kill you this very instant?

298
27:52.609 --> 27:55.528
You Josenjing vermin.

299
28:00.241 --> 28:04.454
I made you who you are, and now you're going to bite your own master?

300
28:12.796 --> 28:14.422
He's persistent.

301
28:17.383 --> 28:18.218
Hey.

302
28:18.718 --> 28:20.595
Did you catch all that?

303
28:23.640 --> 28:26.768
Twisted joints and broken bones won't kill him.

304
28:28.436 --> 28:30.021
Don't kill him too easily.

305
28:31.272 --> 28:32.607
Yes, I'll make sure of it.

306
28:33.358 --> 28:34.818
This is morphine.

307
28:35.360 --> 28:37.487
Make sure he lasts until he talks.

308
28:38.738 --> 28:41.199
Damn Josenjing vermin.

309
28:43.117 --> 28:44.494
Please don't kill me.

310
28:56.923 --> 28:58.716
Do you think

311
29:00.635 --> 29:02.345
I'm still the guy I was back then?

312
29:07.809 --> 29:09.894
Shunsuke was child number what again?

313
29:10.687 --> 29:13.481
You've spread your seed around so much, you can't even remember

314
29:13.565 --> 29:16.901
which broodmare Shunsuke came from or what number bastard he was, can you?

315
29:18.278 --> 29:22.448
A notorious serial killer who could have plummeted your company's stock prices,

316
29:24.284 --> 29:25.326
and I quietly…

317
29:28.162 --> 29:29.497
got rid of him for you.

318
29:31.875 --> 29:33.793
That was the condition of our agreement.

319
29:33.877 --> 29:36.754
Strictly speaking, it wasn't you.

320
29:37.547 --> 29:38.423
It was

321
29:39.591 --> 29:43.136
those two detectives who got rid of him.

322
29:47.599 --> 29:48.600
Hey.

323
29:49.434 --> 29:51.102
Please continue.

324
29:52.145 --> 29:55.773
Frankly, the reason Shunsuke became a monster…

325
29:57.442 --> 29:58.985
It was you, wasn't it?

326
30:16.377 --> 30:18.630
It's more potent than poppies or opium.

327
30:20.965 --> 30:23.760
How about we do a clinical trial?

328
30:25.011 --> 30:25.970
Or…

329
30:27.513 --> 30:29.140
you keep your promise.

330
30:30.391 --> 30:31.976
You motherfucker.

331
30:47.075 --> 30:51.496
KOWLOON HOTEL FRONT DESK KASAHARA REINA

332
30:53.706 --> 30:56.250
Excuse me.

333
30:58.836 --> 31:00.046
Kasahara Reina.

334
31:17.271 --> 31:18.815
You look tired.

335
31:19.691 --> 31:20.817
So,

336
31:21.401 --> 31:23.319
did the contract go through all right?

337
31:27.657 --> 31:28.658
Yes.

338
31:30.660 --> 31:33.538
All that hard work's finally paying off. Congratulations.

339
31:34.038 --> 31:36.874
I'll move things forward as soon as you give me the contract.

340
31:36.958 --> 31:37.875
Yoon-ok.

341
31:41.462 --> 31:43.464
How did Kim manage…

342
31:46.092 --> 31:47.760
to get away so easily?

343
31:50.930 --> 31:52.056
I'm sorry, sir.

344
31:53.224 --> 31:55.351
I left all our boys behind. I was sure they'd--

345
31:55.435 --> 31:57.020
That's not what I'm saying.

346
31:59.981 --> 32:03.026
The Korean police are on the move. I'll make sure our boys keep--

347
32:03.109 --> 32:04.610
That's not it either.

348
32:10.366 --> 32:12.535
You never make mistakes like that.

349
32:16.956 --> 32:17.874
Ever.

350
33:14.597 --> 33:15.765
I…

351
37:24.013 --> 37:29.018
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
